## What it does

`packages/catalog` defines a private catalog with Alchemy Domain.
An Item aggregate owns the observations and decisions for one canonical HTTP or HTTPS URL.
An aggregate commits its events and state together in one Durable Object.

Operators send `RecordSighting`, `Keep`, and `Drop` through one Api.
`apps/catalog` hosts that Api with bearer-token authentication.
Recording a decision never publishes content.
The public site receives no catalog data.

## The standard

- The event log is authoritative. `ItemHistory` is a rebuildable summary and cursor-paged event history.
- The first sighting from each source on each UTC day wins. Retrying with another command id adds no observation.
- Item kinds are repo, post, video, and news. An observed item's kind cannot change.
- Keep and Drop require a sighting. An opposite decision can follow; repeating the current decision records nothing.
- Unknown metrics stay absent. A missing measurement never becomes zero.
- Every command and history read requires the operator token. Missing or empty configuration denies access.
- Domain's Api defines this model's contract. Its own projections expose the same schemas and authorization.

This first slice has no cross-item queries, projection database, people, or backfill.
History state holds the latest observation and decision; `ItemHistory.list` pages through earlier events by cursor.
Operators pass an explicit `take` on every list call and resume with its cursor.
Domain beta.87 supplies no default or maximum page size for `View.list`; omitting `take` reads the item's full history.
This slice accepts that limitation for private operator access. Future cross-item Queries must bound every read.
Reads can use a command receipt as `atLeast` to wait for their own write.

## How to check

Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/catalog test` for command stories and generated idempotency histories.
The declaration test expects `Domain.verify(Catalog)` to return no problems.

Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/catalog-server test` for authentication, command retries, and history pagination over `Domain.InMemory`.
Run `pnpm env:check`, then `pnpm turbo run check test build` for the full fence.

Review `pnpm infra:plan` before deployment.
The owner provisions `CATALOG_OPERATOR_TOKEN`; no secret value ships in source.
After deployment, confirm an unauthenticated command and history read fail, then send a synthetic observation with an operator token.
